course: dictionary
lesson: 7852
title: Plants we eat
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: A word can name a kind of plant part. Look for clues around the word radish. «Radishes can be ready in about four weeks, so they suit a first garden» tells you they grow quickly.
explain: The next clue is «the part we eat is a swollen root». A root is the part of a plant that grows under the soil, and swollen means puffed out and fatter than usual. So a radish is a swollen root that we eat.
explain: The first sentence lists other plant parts we eat: seeds, stems, fruit and roots. To check your meaning, swap it in: «the root of a radish» still makes sense when you think of a radish as a root vegetable.
fact: A radish is a small, crunchy root vegetable.
fact: Radishes are often red on the outside and white on the inside.
fact: A radish has a hot, peppery taste, and it is usually eaten raw in salads.
fact: Radishes grow quickly from seed, in about four weeks, so they are good for class gardens.
fact: «A bunch of radishes» means several radishes held or tied together.
exercise: «Radishes can be ready in about four weeks, so they suit a first garden.» How long do radishes take to be ready? | About four years | A day | About a year and a half | *About four weeks
exercise: What is a radish? | *A small, crunchy root vegetable | A kind of bird that lives near water | A tall tree with sweet fruit
exercise: «The part we eat is a swollen root.» What does swollen mean here? | Cold and wet | Thin and dry | *Puffed out and fatter than usual | Bright red paint
test: What colour is a radish usually on the outside? | *Red | Yellow | Blue | Green
test: How do people usually eat radishes? | Cooked in a pie | *Raw in salads | Dried as crisps | Frozen in ice
exam: Which part of a radish do we eat? | The flower | *The swollen root | The seed | The leaf
